{% block contenu %}
<h1>Example 3 — <span class="mot-latin">Lux fulgebit</span></h1>
<p class="chapeau">
    The entrance chant of the dawn Mass at Christmas. A chant of half-light, all
    delicacy&nbsp;: the perfect occasion to hear the <strong>nuances of duration</strong>.
</p>

<div class="fiche">
    <dl>
        <dt>Genre</dt><dd>Introit (entrance chant)</dd>
        <dt>Occasion</dt><dd>Mass at dawn on Christmas Day (<span class="mot-latin">in aurora</span>), in the early morning of 25 December</dd>
        <dt>Text</dt><dd>After Isaiah (Is 9, 2 and 9, 6) and psalm 92</dd>
        <dt>Mode</dt><dd>Mode VIII (<em>sol</em> mode, peaceful and settled)</dd>
        <dt>Style</dt><dd>Neumatic and measured&nbsp;: ideal for observing durations</dd>
        <dt>In the <em>Triplex</em></dt><dd>p. 44</dd>
    </dl>
</div>

<div class="lecteur-audio">
